CAT = "dkmcMotorway"; SEG = "MWY"
# Afsnit 7.16 to 7.21: motorways and expressways, riding beside others, stopping and parking, darkness, light rail.
Q = [
("What is the most common kind of accident for motorcyclists on motorways and their slip roads?",
 "Single-vehicle crashes", ["Head-on collisions", "Crashes with pedestrians", "Crashes at level crossings"],
 "The most common accident type for motorcyclists on motorways and their slip roads is the single-vehicle crash. Other common ones are being hit from behind and running into the vehicle ahead."),
("Your friend rides a large moped (stor knallert) and wants to follow you onto the motorway. May they?",
 "No, large mopeds are banned", ["Yes, in the right-hand lane", "Yes, with dipped beam on", "Yes, if it can do 45 km/h"],
 "Large mopeds must not use motorways or expressways. Only motor vehicles that can lawfully do at least 50 km/h may use a motorway."),
("On a combined entry and exit lane, the broken edge line runs right through without a break. Which rule applies as you move onto the motorway?",
 "The lane-change rule", ["The merging rule", "The right-hand rule", "Motorway traffic must stop"],
 "On a combined entry and exit lane you may merge in turn if the broken edge line ends. If it runs right through without a break, the lane-change rule applies."),
("You ride down an acceleration lane to join a motorway. How should you join?",
 "Accelerate firmly to traffic speed", ["Join at 60 km/h and speed up later", "Stop at the end and wait", "Cross straight to the middle lane"],
 "Use the acceleration lane to build up speed decisively, signal left, slot into a suitable gap and quickly match the speed of motorway traffic."),
("The motorway traffic gives you no gap and the acceleration lane is ending. What should you do?",
 "Slow down and wait for a gap", ["Force your way in", "Ride on along the hard shoulder", "Stop and push the bike back"],
 "If you cannot join, check behind, warn with your brake light, slow down and if necessary stop with as much free acceleration lane ahead as possible, then wait for a chance."),
("Where is the Motorway ends sign (E 44) normally put up?",
 "Where the motorway itself ends", ["At every exit lane", "At each rest area", "Before every slip road"],
 "The Motorway ends sign is normally set up only where the motorway itself ends, not at the exits."),
("Why should you leave larger safety margins on a motorway than on ordinary roads?",
 "Speeds are higher", ["Lanes are narrower", "Bends are sharper", "Lights are dimmer"],
 "At motorway speeds, signal earlier, start manoeuvres sooner, steer more gently and brake more carefully than on an ordinary road."),
("You plan to leave the motorway at the next exit. When should you slow down?",
 "In the exit lane, not before", ["Before you signal right", "On the motorway near the exit", "Only after the exit bend"],
 "Signal right in good time, move into the exit lane at its start and avoid slowing down on the motorway itself, especially with traffic close behind."),
("On an expressway (motortrafikvej), what may you meet at a junction that you would not meet on a motorway?",
 "Traffic crossing the road", ["Vehicles entering from slip roads", "Lorries in the right lane", "Signs for the next exit"],
 "Expressways can have junctions where both drivers and pedestrians may cross the road. Expect crossing traffic there, as well as oncoming traffic over the middle where there is no central reservation."),
("It starts to rain on the motorway. May you stop on the hard shoulder to put on your rain gear?",
 "No, stopping there is banned", ["Yes, with hazard lights on", "Yes, for up to 5 minutes", "Yes, if you stand behind the barrier"],
 "Stopping and parking are not allowed on a motorway, its slip roads or the verges, except to call for help at an emergency phone or after a breakdown. Use a rest area."),
("After a long stretch on the motorway you leave for a country road. What should you check often?",
 "Your speedometer", ["Your fuel gauge", "Your rear tyre", "Your mirror angles"],
 "On wide, gently curving motorways you easily underestimate your own speed, and the effect carries on after you leave. Check the speedometer with quick glances."),
("You cross a long, exposed motorway bridge on a gusty day. What do riders often underestimate?",
 "How hard side wind pushes you", ["How cold the air will be", "How long the bridge is", "How fast the cars behind are"],
 "Underestimating the effect of strong side wind on steering is one of the typical errors behind motorcycle crashes on motorways."),
("You ride along beside a queue of cars in the next lane. What crash should you guard against?",
 "A car turning across you", ["A car reversing into you", "A car hitting you from in front", "A car braking behind you"],
 "Motorcyclists riding beside or just behind other vehicles are hit by cars, cyclists and mopeds that suddenly turn left in front of them at junctions."),
("You ride just behind and to the side of a car in the next lane. Why is that a poor place to stay?",
 "You may be in its blind spot", ["Your lights dazzle the driver", "It blocks your speed signs", "You ride in its spray all day"],
 "Every car has blind spots behind its rear pillars that can fully hide a vehicle close behind on the left or right. Do not linger there."),
("Why must you park your motorcycle with care, even for a short stop?",
 "It may fall and hurt others", ["It may be towed at once", "It may drain its battery", "It may block its own lights"],
 "Motorcycles sometimes fall over because they are not parked securely and can then be a danger to other road users. Use firm ground and the stand."),
("May you park your motorcycle at the kerb right beside another parked two-wheeled motorcycle?",
 "Yes, that is allowed", ["No, never beside a vehicle", "Only if it has a sidecar", "Only for 3 minutes"],
 "Parking beside a vehicle at the kerb is banned, except beside a two-wheeled bicycle, a two-wheeled moped or a two-wheeled motorcycle without a sidecar."),
("You park your solo motorcycle along the outer edge of the road after dark. Must its position light be on?",
 "No, it need not be", ["Yes, always", "Only in towns", "Only on busy main roads"],
 "A two-wheeled motorcycle without a sidecar that is parked along the outermost edge of the road in the lighting-up time does not need its position light on."),
("A sign marks a taxi rank (taxiholdeplads). May you stop your motorcycle there to check a map?",
 "No, it is for taxis only", ["Yes, for up to 3 minutes", "Yes, if no taxi waits", "Yes, with hazard lights on"],
 "The bus stop and taxi rank signs (E 31) ban stopping and parking there for other vehicles, including motorcycles and large mopeds."),
("When do motorcyclists have especially many single-vehicle crashes?",
 "In darkness and at dusk", ["In bright midday sun", "In slow-moving town traffic", "On cold, dry mornings"],
 "Many single-vehicle crashes with motorcyclists happen in darkness and twilight, along with crashes into pedestrians, parked cars, animals and objects on the road."),
("On main beam at night you see a car's lights coming towards you. When should you dip?",
 "About 200 to 300 m before it", ["About 30 to 50 m before it", "About 500 m before it", "Only when it flashes its lights"],
 "Dip your lights at a suitable distance, about 200 to 300 m before an oncoming car or motorcycle and about 100 to 150 m before a cyclist or moped rider."),
("You ride on an unlit country road at night. What should set your top speed?",
 "The reach of your headlight", ["The posted limit if it is dry", "The speed of the car ahead", "Your engine's best gear"],
 "Adjust your speed to the reduced view in darkness so that you can stop the motorcycle within the range of your lights."),
("You ride beside a light rail line (letbane) in town. What is the usual top speed of the light rail trains?",
 "Bus speed, at most 80 km/h", ["Always 30 km/h, even outside town", "Up to 130 km/h", "No limit at all on its own track"],
 "Light rail trains follow the speed limits inside and outside built-up areas, but as a rule may not go faster than the limit for buses, at most 80 km/h."),
("You must stop within 2 m of a tram or light rail track. What must you do?",
 "Stay close and move off for trams", ["Leave the bike and go shopping", "Switch on your fog light", "Put a triangle on the track"],
 "If you stop or park on a track or nearer than 2 m to it, stay close enough to notice an approaching train and move your vehicle out of its way at once."),
("Motorway traffic thickens and you ride in a long line of vehicles. What is a typical error behind motorcycle crashes there?",
 "Too short a gap", ["Riding with dipped beam", "Using the left mirror", "Keeping right"],
 "Typical errors on motorways include too short a safety gap in denser traffic and when closing in, misjudging speeds and distances, and overrating the motorcycle."),
]
